// How diffuse each colour's edge is, from the same segmented masks: the Lab of the scan is projected onto the
// direction across the outline, its median profile is taken in 1/3-px bins of the signed distance over +-1 mm and
// normalised by its own two ends, and the width is 1 / (steepest slope) -- for a Gaussian-blurred step, sigma*sqrt(2pi).
// The raster's own step is removed in quadrature, and each colour is then divided by its own sheet's median width,
// because the absolute width carries the scanner's blur (0.55 mm at 5 px/mm against 0.19 mm at 13 px/mm) which
// belongs to the scan and not to the paint. So 1 is a typical edge for its sheet; clamped to 0.5..1.8. The shader
// uses it as the per-layer blur width, so a gall-rich colour has a soft edge and a lean one a crisp edge.
